{{!
    @template local_socialcert/provider_limit_notice

    Alert of the plugin settings page about the usage limit of the Datacurso AI provider.

    The plugin applies no usage limit of its own, so the alert is red, with a button to the provider
    configuration, while the provider limit is off for this plugin, and green with the limit while
    it is on. It is rendered by local_socialcert\local\admin\provider_limit_notice on every load of
    the settings page.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * active bool - True when the provider limit is on for this plugin.
    * limit int - Credits allowed per user and window, only when active.
    * window string - Localized length of the window (e.g. "1 hour"), only when active.
    * configurl string - URL of the provider page where the limit is configured.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "active": false,
        "configurl": "https://example.com/ai/provider/datacurso/admin/report_sections.php?tab=config"
    }
}}
<div class="local_socialcert-provider_limit_notice">
    {{#active}}
    <div class="alert alert-success d-flex align-items-start gap-2 mb-0" role="status">
        {{#pix}} i/valid, core {{/pix}}
        <div>
            <p class="mb-2">{{#str}} providerlimit_active, local_socialcert, { "limit": {{limit}}, "window": {{#quote}}{{window}}{{/quote}} } {{/str}}</p>
            <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-sm" href="{{configurl}}">{{#str}} providerlimit_configure, local_socialcert {{/str}}</a>
        </div>
    </div>
    {{/active}}
    {{^active}}
    <div class="alert alert-danger d-flex align-items-start gap-2 mb-0" role="alert">
        {{#pix}} i/warning, core {{/pix}}
        <div>
            <p class="fw-bold mb-1">{{#str}} providerlimit_missing_title, local_socialcert {{/str}}</p>
            <p class="mb-2">{{#str}} providerlimit_missing, local_socialcert {{/str}}</p>
            <a class="btn btn-danger btn-sm" href="{{configurl}}">{{#str}} providerlimit_configure, local_socialcert {{/str}}</a>
        </div>
    </div>
    {{/active}}
</div>
